{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "A Comedy of Errors", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Let Down", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Expressing Wishes and Regrets ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">I wish</span> or <span class=\"strong\">If only</span> ... to express wishes and regret. </br>You use <span class=\"strong\">wish </span>+ <span class=\"strong\">would</span> +<span class=\"strong\"> infinitive</span> to talk about things you would like to change about a situation or a person.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The verb <span class=\"italic\">wish </span>introduces an idea. After <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: </br> Wish + Simple Past tense </br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">wish she messaged</span> me more often.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use wish + would about other people who are doing (or not doing) something that you don't like and that you would like to change. You don't normally use it about yourself or about a situation that nobody can change. </br>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">wish you wouldn't keep</span> asking me that.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">If only</span> ... to express wishes in the present or regret about a past action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: </br>If only ... + Simple Past tense = wish</br> If only ... + Past Perfect = regret", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If only I hadn't blocked</span> her online! Now we can never go out again.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I wish you wouldn't ask me that, because the answer, my good man, is always yes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wish she would have messaged me at the very least.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wish I hadn't blocked her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I definitely wish you wouldn't keep asking me that. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If only she had messaged me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " If only this didn't happen", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Expressing Absence of Necessity", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to express absence of necessity in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Absence of necessity is expressed with the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span>, not with mustn't.</br> Example: <ul></br><span class=\"italic\">You don't have to date her if you don't like her. (it is not necessary to date her) </br></br>You mustn't date her. (it is necessary not to date her)</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by the negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To express absence of necessity in the past, you use the structure: subject + didn't + have/need + infinitive", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:</br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">You didn't have to get so</span> upset last night. </br><span class=\"strong\">She didn't need to check</span> her phone constantly during dinner.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She didn't have to be so cruel.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She didn't need to call.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She didn't have to get my hopes up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You didn't need to try so hard to explain yourself and make things right, but you did.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "No, you didn't have to do that.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cold feet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a loss of confidence", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My girlfriend has gotten cold feet about getting married. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear when you get stood up!", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "disrespect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "lack of respect", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should not disrespect your teachers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "jump to conclusions", "type": "name"}, {"content": "make assumptions about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't jump to conclusions. They might not be dating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to bring down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "depress", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The results of the football game really brought me down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "flake", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a worthless person or group of people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She never does what she says she will. She is such a flake.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to steal someone's heart", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause someone to fall in love with oneself.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My neighbor has really stolen my heart.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write a story about a disastrous date.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use wish + simple past to express wishes and regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my story with a partner and receive feedback.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback to my partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write a 250 word story about the most disastrous date you have even been on.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you don't have a personal story, create one. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use wish + simple past to express wishes and regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your story with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Offer feedback for your partner's story.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn10le10ob10re1img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn10le10ob10re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Server</span>: Would the gentleman like some more wine?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I wish you wouldn't ask me that because the answer my good man is always yes.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter, I'm sorry. If only this didn't happen. Is there anything I can do?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: And I definitely wish you wouldn't keep asking me that. I'm kidding, V. Thanks for your concern. I have a question for you though.  How many times have you been stood up in the past?"}, {"image": "engenn10le10ob10re2img02.jpg", "time": "26000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: A couple. Everyone has. I'm sorry this person has stolen your heart like this. She didn't have to be so cruel.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Man, I wish she wouldn't have stood me up this time. She didn't have to get my hopes up.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Maybe she just got cold feet? Did you send her a message?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yes, several with my number. She didn't need to call, but a text message would be nice.  I wish she would have messaged me at the very least. If only she had messaged me.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You know what? You didn't need to try so hard to explain yourself and make things right, but you did.   Anyone who disrespects you this much is scum. Block her from your profile right now."}, {"image": "engenn10le10ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "71200", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: But Vanessa, I have to keep the lines of communication open. We shouldn't jump to conclusions. She might be lost or on her way. If only she texted me.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter, dump her ... now!\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:   Ok. Ok. See? Happy?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes. Hello? Yes ... No, you didn't have to do that. They'll be fine \u2026 They did what? Peter, I'll be back soon. Don't let this bring you down. Ok?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Ok. I wish I hadn't blocked her, maybe I can get her unblocked."}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le10ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le10ob10re1img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about relationships and use colloquial expressions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express wishes and regrets.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express what is not necessary. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How do you feel before you go on a first date 